<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Rendered by scripts/build_app.sh, which fills in the version, the bundle identifier (MCAP_BUNDLE_ID) and the two names of the app: the human name
  (MCAP_APP_NAME, the display name and the name in the usage strings) and the file-safe short name (MCAP_APP_SHORT_NAME, the app folder, the executable and
  CFBundleName); scripts/bundle_id.sh holds the defaults and validates both before they get here. Keep this file deterministic (no build dates).
  The Korean sentences put a fixed word after the name instead of a particle, so they read right for any name.
  Only when MCAP_BUILT_BY is set does build_app.sh add a builder key and a builder line to NSHumanReadableCopyright
  (docs/BRANDING.md); this template itself never names a builder.
  An ad-hoc signed app has the code hash as its identity for macOS privacy permissions, so any change to this file
  or to the binary makes macOS ask for the permissions again; an app signed with the local identity
  (scripts/make_signing_identity.sh) keeps them.

  Icon: CFBundleIconFile=AppIcon names Contents/Resources/AppIcon.icns, which scripts/build_app.sh copies from
  app/Resources/AppIcon.icns (generated by scripts/make_icon.swift). macOS shows it in notifications, System Settings and
  Finder; without it every notification of the app carries a blank generic icon. There is no CFBundleIconName on purpose:
  that key points into an asset catalog (Assets.car, built by actool from Xcode), and this project is built with swiftc only.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>CFBundleDevelopmentRegion</key>
	<string>en</string>
	<key>CFBundleExecutable</key>
	<string>@APP_SHORT_NAME@</string>
	<key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
	<string>@BUNDLE_ID@</string>
	<key>CFBundleInfoDictionaryVersion</key>
	<string>6.0</string>
	<key>CFBundleIconFile</key>
	<string>AppIcon</string>
	<key>CFBundleName</key>
	<string>@APP_SHORT_NAME@</string>
	<key>CFBundleDisplayName</key>
	<string>@APP_NAME@</string>
	<key>CFBundlePackageType</key>
	<string>APPL</string>
	<key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>
	<string>@VERSION@</string>
	<key>CFBundleVersion</key>
	<string>@VERSION@</string>
	<key>NSHumanReadableCopyright</key>
	<string>Copyright 2026 Meeting Capture contributors</string>
	<key>LSMinimumSystemVersion</key>
	<string>14.4</string>
	<key>LSUIElement</key>
	<true/>
	<key>LSApplicationCategoryType</key>
	<string>public.app-category.productivity</string>
	<key>NSSupportsAutomaticTermination</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSSupportsSuddenTermination</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSHighResolutionCapable</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>@APP_NAME@ records your own voice from the microphone during online meetings (Zoom, Teams, Google Meet) so the meeting can be transcribed. By default the audio stays on this Mac and is transcribed locally; the transcript text, the meeting title and your vocabulary are sent to Anthropic to write the note. Optional speech engines that you enable can send audio to the server you configure. / @APP_NAME@ 앱은 온라인 회의(Zoom, Teams, Google Meet) 중 내 목소리를 마이크로 녹음하여 전사합니다. 기본 설정에서 오디오는 이 Mac 안에서만 로컬로 전사되며, 회의록 작성을 위해 전사 텍스트, 회의 제목, 용어 목록이 Anthropic으로 전송됩니다. 사용자가 켠 선택적 음성 인식 엔진은 설정한 서버로 오디오를 보낼 수 있습니다.</string>
	<key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
	<string>@APP_NAME@ records the audio played by this Mac (the other participants' voices) during online meetings so the meeting can be transcribed locally. Video and screen contents are never recorded. / @APP_NAME@ 앱은 온라인 회의 중 이 Mac에서 재생되는 소리(상대방 음성)를 녹음하여 로컬에서 전사합니다. 화면이나 영상은 녹화하지 않습니다.</string>
	<key>NSAppleEventsUsageDescription</key>
	<string>@APP_NAME@ asks Google Chrome for the address and title of open tabs to recognize that a Google Meet call is in progress (it never reads page contents). / @APP_NAME@ 앱은 Google Meet 통화 중인지 확인하기 위해 Google Chrome의 열린 탭 주소와 제목을 조회합니다(페이지 내용은 읽지 않습니다).</string>
</dict>
</plist>
